  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a consistent pathway where Protein C interacts with E-selectin, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including Batilol, cocaine, and Methylconiine, all of which ultimately target GR-ST. This indicates that GR-ST is a downstream effector of E-selectin, and Protein C serves as a central node in the interaction network leading to GR-ST. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with some variation in the strength of the evidence across the different compounds. The mechanism appears to involve E-selectin as a key mediator, with Protein C acting as a common upstream target. The presence of multiple compounds targeting E-selectin and ultimately GR-ST supports the idea that GR-ST is a downstream target of these interactions, and that Protein C is a central component in this pathway.",
